Description: GHSA-r6x9-5r99-36j7 (the 2026 partial fix) for PHP 5.6, on top of the GHSA-h35g-vwh6-m678 (CVE-2024-8929) fix that Remi's 5.6 branch now has: a hostile or man-in-the-middle MySQL server could still make the mysqlnd client read past the end of a received packet and leak heap bytes into PHP-visible values. php_mysqlnd_net_field_length() takes the bytes left in the packet and returns MYSQLND_INVALID_NET_FIELD_LENGTH when a length-encoded integer would read past them, php_mysqlnd_net_field_length_ll() returns an optional value that the callers check, and every packet reader checks the bytes left before a read (BAIL_IF_NOT_ENOUGH_DATA_EX) instead of after it (BAIL_IF_NO_MORE_DATA): greeting (server version and plugin name found with memchr, both scramble parts bounded), auth response and change-user (the auth switch plugin name found with memchr), OK, EOF, result-set header, column definition (name lengths and the fixed block), prepare response and sha256 public key; the "shorter than expected" warnings no longer print a byte count computed past the packet. The EOF of a text row needs its 4 status bytes, the prepared-statement value decoders give the length decoder the bytes left in the row and reject a length it cannot read, the BIT value of a text row is bounded by the space reserved from the column length, and the prepared-statement EOF reset releases the connection reference and the command buffer before its memset. Every check of the branch stays (the h35g fix with its auth_protocol and binary row follow-ups, the minimum lengths of temporal fields, the OK message past the packet body); only its OK length-prefix check is done by the bounded length decoder now. 31 tests for the fake MySQL server of the branch: ext/mysqli/tests/fake_server.inc gains the packets they need and starts the server with exec, so that proc_terminate() stops the server and not only the shell.
Origin: azsupport, port of php-src commit 2af14de0f223 (Partial Fix GHSA-r6x9-5r99-36j7, Jakub Zelenka and Nora Dossche, 12.07.2026) of the PHP 7.4 security branch of Remi Collet (remicollet/php-src-security PHP-7.4-security-backports), rebuilt on Remi's 5.6 branch f98c3c2b (17.11.2026), which has the GHSA-h35g-vwh6-m678 fix (dae0e5c, a cherry-pick of php-src 2f5aa9f9d150, with ec0107a) and Ondřej Surý's 5.6 follow-ups c3279aa, 7a82a61 and f10baba; of our earlier port of 2f5aa9f9d150, only what the branch lacks is kept

